  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Natural resources conservation and livelihoods innovation for disadvantaged people in Maizegzeg, Eth</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">An innovative livelihoods learning initiative with ADCS, it follows a very successful pilot carried out in the Maizegzeg watershed of Degua Tembien district in central Tigray.  This project will: reduced soil erosion, reclaim degraded hillsides and gullies for productive use, increase the productivity of farmers&#x2019; plots and increased income, provide water and sanitation and provide a test bed for pilot initiatives for government and other NGOs.  There will also be a significant element of skills development for ADCS staff charged with implementing this novel and ambitious project.  27,500 beneficiaries are targeted.  The four year project worth nearly 740,000 pounds is co-funded by the Big Lottery Fund and Tr&#xf3;caire.</narrative>
  </description>
